- add a bitfield class and use it for move and hash node

### Changed
- change some types, and special types for move, evalscore, bitbase, and hash
  internal data
- use Board::bitboardPieceType
- use default member initialization for board and engine
- don't keep white psqt and outpost in memory
- simplification in movegen

## 3.2.0 (2023-12-09)
### Fixed
- fix precision when saving tuning variables in text file
- fix some clang tidy warnings
- fix enums in move.h to pass undefined sanitizer, and use prefix operator++
- fix missing const in pv and moveorder
- fix node type in YBWC split
- fix thread variable name in lazysmp
- fix best move update in iterative deepening
- fix missing or unused includes
- fix mersenne twister initialization
- use const for lmr and lmp tables
- remove special characters in config file lines
- fix possible crashes in command line or config file, and simplifications 
  in module.cpp
- simplifications in evaluation, and fix a warning with bitboards in 32bit 
  version
- fix a draw detection problem

### Added
- add a function to simplify LMR table lookup
- replace tablebase code by Fathom
- new tuner using Gradient Descent
- add new pawn shield and storm, bishop outpost, and passed pawns bonus by file
- add more unit tests
- add sanitizer options with cmake

### Changed
- replace most of #define by constexpr
- use a reference for Tunable
- don't access items by index in ConfigFile
- generate mvv/lva table at compile time
- move ChessSearchStack declaration in search.h
- use a reference of ChessMoveSortList in ChessMoveOrder, and declare it in 
  ChessSearchStack, to reduce stack memory usage and not zero initializing the 
  move array in the search functions
- create a structure for search data (repetition, search stack, and pv), and
  declare it in thread to reduce stack memory usage
- use std::thread, and remove thread.h/.cpp
- use final on protocol classes
- use a template with node type for search functions
- rename evaluation parameters and use EvalScore for most of them, add a
  function to generate parameters declaration in C++ code
- Eval penality for pawns and trapped pieces are now negative numbers. Add 
  new personality parameters : outpost, passed pawns, and pawn shield.
- simplifications in evaluate, and change pawn shield evaluation
- change endgame scaling and tempo
- change LMR and LMP conditions
- simplify move ordering code
- use more std algorithms, and Move MaterialMask and move list in separate files
- simplify bitboards, and calculate some arrays at compile time

